From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: TurboVadim <yolkin.vadim@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:27:22 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Cache immutable brain memory snapshots and accessors

Cache Optional snapshots by slot value identity and one immutable accessor
per declarative condition kind in the owning brain's MemorySlot. Clear
accessors on identity replacement and clear, including expiry. Shared
behavior nodes retain no brains or snapshots. Preserve trigger order,
unregistered memories, retained accessor reads and writes, and TTL semantics.

With indexed gate traversal, eight interleaved villagers pairs change
main-thread allocation from 671.389 to 559.389 KB/t,
-16.68% +/-2.79 points at 95% confidence. Tick time is
1.147 to 1.115 mspt, -2.82% +/-7.80 points.
No digest drift. All 11 selected tests pass, including shared-node writes
from two threads, node retention, snapshot and ordered lifecycle checks.

